{
  "On a tablet and a phone a layout of groups, splits and dock areas does not fit as it is. The manager keeps the layout and shows it another way: the same documents, groups and areas, the same saved JSON, the content moved and never made again. It goes by its own width, not by the device; on a touch screen its tabs and buttons get larger.": "",
  "Three ways to show one layout": "",
  "The layout as it is: groups side by side and one under the other, dock areas around them, floating windows, new browser windows.": "",
  "At most two groups side by side: the first branch of the layout on one side, the rest on the other, each showing the group used last; the groups that do not fit fold as tabs into the strip of the group beside them (their tabs keep their own group: a tap activates that group there). Dock areas become drawers from their edge, the bottom one a sheet, opened from their titles along the edges or by a finger swiping in from the edge. A floating window is a large sheet.": "",
  "One document, full screen. Above it a bar: its title (a swipe left or right goes to the document beside it, a tap opens its commands in an action sheet), its close button and the number of open documents, which opens the list of them. Tools of the dock areas are buttons in a bar at the bottom: a tap opens a sheet (peek, half, full by its handle; swipe down closes it), or a drawer for an area that asks for one. A floating window is a full-screen sheet. New browser windows are off; the tab menu is an action sheet.": "",
  "Pick one: the layout under it does not change. Save the layout in each presentation: the JSON is the same.": "",
  "With `presentation: 'auto'` (the default) the manager watches its own width and the screen's pointer. Under `phoneWidth` (560) it shows as on a phone, whatever the pointer: phones are 360 to 430 pixels wide, while a manager of about 590 beside a desktop page's side column stays a desktop. Under `tabletWidth` (1024) it shows as on a tablet when the screen is a touch screen; with a mouse it stays a desktop (`tabletWhen: 'width'` lets the width alone decide). An app changes both limits to fit its layout. Drag the frame's corner: what you type in the note and how far a file is scrolled stay.": "",
  "Settings and events": "",
  "Every part is a setting, live: how dock areas show on each (an area may say its own), the swipe from an edge, the back button, how the tab menus show. `onPresentationChanging` can refuse a change.": "",
  "The phone's list of documents": "",
  "Shows that document and closes the list.": "",
  "Closes the document (asking as `onClosing` says; a document that may only be hidden is hidden). Let go early, it goes back.": "",
  "Lifts the row: drag it up or down its group, or into another group's section; let go to move the document there (`onMoving` / `onMoved`).": "",
  "Opens the document's commands in an action sheet.": "",
  "Filters by title and description.": "",
  "Between the rows; Enter shows the document.": "",
  "Closes it; moves it a place up or down (past an end, into the group before or after); opens its commands.": "",
  "The back button": "",
  "Android's back button and the browser's back gesture go through the session history. Each sheet, drawer and list holds one entry while it is open and takes it back when it closes otherwise, so no entry is left behind; the manager holds one while it can go back through its documents.": "",
  "Back": "",
  "The back button closes the one on top.": "",
  "It goes back to the document before (`goBack`), as long as there is one.": "",
  "It is the browser's again: the page goes back.": "",
  "How the layout shows: by the manager's own width, or always one way.": "",
  "Under this width (in pixels of the manager, not of the screen) `auto` shows it as on a phone, whatever the pointer.": "",
  "`'touch'`: the tablet layout only when the screen's pointer is a finger (`(pointer: coarse)`, followed live); with a mouse a narrow manager stays a desktop until it is under `phoneWidth`. `'width'`: the width alone.": "",
  "How the documents' groups' bars look on a tablet or a phone: with the `compact…` settings (no scroll buttons, shrinking tabs, small buttons, a single document as a title), as in the dock areas; `'documents'` keeps the desktop bar. Change the `compact…` props to change that look.": "",
  "How dock areas show on a phone; an area's own `phoneDockMode` wins.": "",
  "How dock areas show on a tablet: `auto` is a drawer for the sides and the top, a sheet for the bottom. An area's own `tabletDockMode` wins.": "",
  "On a tablet or a phone a finger swiping in from an edge opens the dock area there, as a drawer.": "",
  "On a phone the browser's back goes back through the documents once nothing is open on top.": "",
  "How the tab menus show; `null`: an action sheet on a phone, a sheet for a finger on a tablet, a menu on a desktop.": "",
  "`{ from, to, width, cancel }`: refused, the layout keeps showing as it does until the width or the setting changes again.": "",
  "How it shows now: `'desktop'`, `'tablet'` or `'phone'`.": "",
  "On a phone: opens or closes the list of open documents. `documentListOpen` is reactive.": "",
  "On a tablet or a phone: opens a dock area's drawer or sheet with that document shown, or closes it. `activate(doc)` of a tool or of a document in a floating window opens its drawer or sheet too.": "",
  "The area's own setting; `null` follows the manager.": "",
  "unchanged": "",
  "Work as on a desktop and change the layout; it is shown the way the presentation allows. `moveToNewWindow` returns `null` on a phone.": "",
  "The drawers and sheets are the kit's [Drawer](/drawer) and [BottomSheet](/bottomsheet), the action sheet its [ActionSheet](/actionsheet).": ""
}
